<p>Lebanese and Israeli envoys are due to meet in Washington on April 23 in US-hosted talks aimed at extending a 10-day ceasefire set to expire on April 26. Beirut says it wants more time to stop the violence and open a broader negotiating track on an Israeli withdrawal from southern Lebanon, the return of Lebanese detainees held in Israel, and border issues. The talks offer a narrow but meaningful diplomatic opening after the truce sharply reduced violence, even though clashes have continued. At the same time, Lebanon is protesting Israeli demolitions of homes in parts of southern Lebanon that Israeli forces have occupied since the ceasefire began, warning that the destruction could leave displaced residents with little to return to if the truce holds. Israel says Hezbollah used the buildings as outposts, while Hezbollah said it carried out a drone attack after what it called Israeli ceasefire violations. Lebanon also reported fresh Israeli strikes in the south that killed several people on April 23. Israeli Foreign Minister Gideon Saar said Hezbollah remains the main obstacle to peace and normalization between the two countries.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ju40B4NoVPmcDf89SV3XcQushFQpU7hB7b_ekIwlj3DVHTooberHGBO91-q59qgc8VeL5kBX0qkYYczTQNP7lzsP5yTyYYslUeJYwdQDk8DQOgk791JQeFYzHADWyZ70xhxXW4l5lzGvH2kgisaboVyWzU5CRN0D_XttA8u6f7MUA2H4BDQPZ3lg6WRT3VLEMVvCUYzSBs9B5QqO3f8jPUY-EZ1JY99GZMkvMRvAqx2Xbt0wNDK5LOY75Q5PH6PWdaVJIOMaawBEA3GFkA' alt='Israeli army vehicles and bulldozers operate in southern Lebanon, April 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Next phase: A Lebanese official said Beirut sees any ceasefire extension as a necessary first step before talks can move beyond ambassadors to negotiations on a withdrawal, detainees, and land-border delineation.</li><li>State pressure: A deputy director at the Carnegie Endowment’s Middle East Center told Semafor that the actions of Israel and Hezbollah are &quot;converging in undermining the Lebanese state&quot;.</li><li>Journalist killed: Dawn reported that one of the five people killed in fresh Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon on Wednesday was a journalist.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanese government: President Joseph Aoun said Beirut&#x27;s envoy would seek both a ceasefire extension and a halt to Israeli demolitions in southern villages, underscoring Lebanon&#x27;s effort to tie immediate calm to conditions that would allow civilians to return. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994209/lebanon-israel-to-meet-today-as-truce-hangs-by-a-thread'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israeli government: Israel says the homes being destroyed were used by Hezbollah as outposts, and Foreign Minister Gideon Saar said Hezbollah is blocking peace and normalization between the two countries. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-lebanon-israel-war-ceasefire-talks/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: The group said it launched an attack drone at an Israeli artillery position in southern Lebanon in response to what it described as an Israeli ceasefire violation. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1994209/lebanon-israel-to-meet-today-as-truce-hangs-by-a-thread'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>UN peacekeepers: UN peacekeepers have grown increasingly worried that the scale of demolitions in occupied southern areas could prevent many displaced residents from returning even if the truce survives. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3351107/lebanon-confront-israel-over-demolition-homes-occupied-areas-ceasefire'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>Regional analysts: An expert cited by Semafor argued that Beirut risks being squeezed between Israel and Hezbollah, weakening the Lebanese state even during ceasefire diplomacy. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/23/2026/lebanon-truce-threatened-ahead-of-talks'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3351107/lebanon-confront-israel-over-demoliti